test_command=for t in tests/*_test.sh; do sh "$t" || exit 1; done
id=quoting-01 result=green reason=unit test "quoting-01: all four agents' rendered descriptions are double-quoted YAML scalars on both clients, value byte-preserved from agents/meta" in tests/description-quoting_test.sh passes (every rendered agent file's description line starts with `description: "` and ends with `"` with nothing after it, and the unquoted value equals agents/meta/<role>.yaml's description byte-for-byte)
id=quoting-02 result=green reason=unit test "quoting-02: both /antz-set-model renders carry a double-quoted description line (third quoting site)" in tests/description-quoting_test.sh passes (render_set_model_command's short_desc is emitted as a double-quoted single-line scalar in both clients' antz-set-model.md; the /antz command renderers stay unquoted, out of scope per the sub-spec)
id=quoting-03 result=green reason=three unit tests in tests/description-quoting_test.sh, one per Examples row, pass: "quoting-03 (Says \"hi\"): embedded quotes escape to \" on all three sites...", "quoting-03 (back\\slash): embedded backslash escapes to \\\\ on all three sites...", "quoting-03 (a \"b\" \\ c): mixed quotes+backslash escape per YAML rules on all three sites..." (each stages its raw value into every meta description AND both install.sh short_desc assignments, renders --all, and asserts every description line is exactly description: <rendered> at render_claude, render_opencode and render_set_model_command on both clients)
id=quoting-04 result=green reason=unit test "quoting-04: unquoting every rendered description line reproduces its source byte-for-byte (all agents, both set-model renders, escape-heavy round-trip)" in tests/description-quoting_test.sh passes (an awk left-to-right unescape independent of install.sh's sed escaping recovers agents/meta/*.yaml and the eval'd short_desc sources verbatim, plus a staged round-trip of it's "x" \y\ :d with quotes, backslashes, a trailing backslash, an apostrophe, and colon+space)
id=quoting-05 result=green reason=unit test "quoting-05: renderinject-01/02/05 byte-identity re-scoped quoting-aware with loud notes (structural assertions kept), render-03/render-04-scoping re-scoped to the current renderer, full unit suite green" in tests/description-quoting_test.sh passes (static half: renderinject_test.sh carries the loud hardening-installsh (sub-spec 02, quoting) re-scope note and its dequote_description normalization with the reconstruction and frontmatter-shape structural assertions still present and enforced; skills-activation-render_test.sh carries the 02-quoting note that render-03/render-04-scoping compare against a controlled mutation of the working install.sh so no stale pre-quoting byte-identity survives; dynamic half: the other 28 tests/*_test.sh suites all run to zero failures)
